SUMMARY:Tampopo (1985)
LOCATION:Tomorrow Theater\, 1219 SW Park Ave\, Portland OR
GEO:45.5158;-122.6831
DESCRIPTION:Dir. Jūzō Itami · 115 min\n\nIn this humorous paean to the j
 oys of food\, a pair of truck drivers happen onto a decrepit roadside shop
  selling ramen noodles. The widowed owner\, Tampopo\, begs them to help he
 r turn her establishment into a paragon of the "art of noodle-soup making"
 . Interspersed are satirical vignettes about the importance of food to dif
 ferent aspects of human life.\n\nTickets: https://tomorrowtheater.org/show
 times/tampopo-11-15-26-700-pm/\n\nMore showtimes: https://mattlohkamp.gith
 ub.io/small-screens-pdx/
